Currently all options are passed a fixed `Text` for their name. Sometimes, especially in the case of buttons, it would be nice to change their text. I propose updating the option implementations and builders to use a `Supplier<Text>` instead. This change would also easily be backwards compatible.

To demonstrate take this simple example:

This is currently possible:
```java
AtomicBoolean added = new AtomicBoolean(false);
ButtonOption.createBuilder()
    .name(Text.literal("Add or Remove"))
    .action((scr, opt) -> {
        if(added.get()) {
            added.set(false);
        } else {
            added.set(true);
        }
    });
```

This would be possible with the proposal:
```java
AtomicBoolean added = new AtomicBoolean(false);
ButtonOption.createBuilder()
    .name(() => added.get() ? Text.literal("Remove") : Text.literal("Add"))
    .action((scr, opt) -> {
        if(added.get()) {
            added.set(false);
        } else {
            added.set(true);
        }
    });
```

You currently cannot start typing a negative number in a `NumberFieldController`, you can work around this by typing the absolute value then prepending a `-` afterwards.

Seems like this was previously an issue: https://github.com/isXander/YetAnotherConfigLib/issues/72, but has been re-introduced.

A suggested fix would be:
```java
@Override
public boolean isInputValid(String input) {
    if (min() < 0 && "-".equals(input)) {
        return true;
    }
    
    input = input.replace(DECIMAL_FORMAT_SYMBOLS.getGroupingSeparator() + "", "");
    ParsePosition parsePosition = new ParsePosition(0);
    NUMBER_FORMAT.parse(input, parsePosition);
    return parsePosition.getIndex() == input.length();
}
```

